 $\\frac{d}{dx}(yI(x))=I(x)Q(x),$ where $I(x)$ is an integrating factor." :question/worked-solution "First, we write the equation in standard form. This gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}+\\left(6 x\\right)\\cdot y=x e^{- 3 x^{2}}.\n$$\n\nThis equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}+P(x)y=Q(x)\n$$\n\nwith $P(x)=6 x$ and $Q(x)=x e^{- 3 x^{2}}.$ We proceed to find an integrating factor $I(x)$ using the definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & =e^{\\int P(x)\\,dx} \\\\  & =e^{\\int \\left(6 x\\right)\\,dx} \\\\  & =e^{3 x^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply our differential equation through by $I(x)=e^{3 x^{2}}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\left(e^{3 x^{2}}\\right)\\cdot \\left(\\frac{dy}{dx}+\\left(6 x\\right)\\cdot y\\right) & =\\left(e^{3 x^{2}}\\right)\\cdot \\left(x e^{- 3 x^{2}}\\right) \\\\ \\left(e^{3 x^{2}}\\right)\\cdot \\frac{dy}{dx}+\\left(6 x\\right)\\cdot \\left(e^{3 x^{2}}\\right)\\cdot y & =\\left(e^{3 x^{2}}\\right)\\cdot \\left(x e^{- 3 x^{2}}\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we rewrite the left hand side as $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y\\cdot I(x)):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(y\\cdot \\left(e^{3 x^{2}}\\right)\\right) & =\\left(e^{3 x^{2}}\\right)\\cdot \\left(x e^{- 3 x^{2}}\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186495346 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "12a0cb4c-5470-5b60-b845-2fea9caa9516" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(y\\cdot \\left(x\\right)\\right)=\\left(x\\right)\\cdot \\left(x^{2}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495314} {:answer/id #uuid "732634a7-b684-5342-875a-b0080faf8912" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(y\\cdot \\left(e^{x}\\right)\\right)=\\left(e^{x}\\right)\\cdot \\left(x^{2}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495335} {:answer/id #uuid "91971313-09d0-59d7-a70f-11595c40eb04" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(y\\cdot \\left(e^{2 x}\\right)\\right)=\\left(e^{2 x}\\right)\\cdot \\left(x^{2}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495344} {:answer/id #uuid "a06cec39-9592-52fd-a2e7-778b2eb94b1a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(y\\cdot \\left(x^{2}\\right)\\right)=\\left(x^{2}\\right)\\cdot \\left(x^{2}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495349} {:answer/id #uuid "c88c1c16-6052-5ee3-ad30-dc668b434dc8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(y\\cdot \\left(e^{- x}\\right)\\right)=\\left(e^{- x}\\right)\\cdot \\left(x^{2}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495360}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "732634a7-b684-5342-875a-b0080faf8912" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(y\\cdot \\left(e^{x}\\right)\\right)=\\left(e^{x}\\right)\\cdot \\left(x^{2}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495335} :answer-field/id #uuid "3060f3c4-885b-5427-ae2c-0db77cc62040" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495323}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "979f5ce5-340c-5f1b-87a2-e39d8a750547" :question/problem "Consider the following first-order linear ODE for the function $y=y(x):$\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}+y=x^{2}\n$$\n\nWrite the equation in the form $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(yI(x))=I(x)Q(x),$ where $I(x)$ is an integrating factor." :question/worked-solution "This equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}+P(x)y=Q(x)\n$$\n\nwith $P(x)=1$ and $Q(x)=x^{2}.$ We proceed to find an integrating factor $I(x)$ using the definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & =e^{\\int P(x)\\,dx} \\\\  & =e^{\\int \\left(1\\right)\\,dx} \\\\  & =e^{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply our differential equation through by $I(x)=e^{x}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\left(e^{x}\\right)\\cdot \\left(\\frac{dy}{dx}+y\\right) & =\\left(e^{x}\\right)\\cdot \\left(x^{2}\\right) \\\\ \\left(e^{x}\\right)\\cdot \\frac{dy}{dx}+\\left(1\\right)\\cdot \\left(e^{x}\\right)\\cdot y & =\\left(e^{x}\\right)\\cdot \\left(x^{2}\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we rewrite the left hand side as $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y\\cdot I(x)):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(y\\cdot \\left(e^{x}\\right)\\right) & =\\left(e^{x}\\right)\\cdot \\left(x^{2}\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186495352 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "06ad0058-543a-56f0-a30b-63445b19fb0b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(y\\cdot \\left(e^{2 x^{2}}\\right)\\right)=\\left(e^{2 x^{2}}\\right)\\cdot \\left(x e^{2 x^{2}}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495313} {:answer/id #uuid "691137d8-cd1d-5c0e-9f2b-2a806bb36f04" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(y\\cdot \\left(e^{- 4 x}\\right)\\right)=\\left(e^{- 4 x}\\right)\\cdot \\left(x e^{2 x^{2}}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495333} {:answer/id #uuid "78cff9f9-81d3-58d9-80de-61ed3308bf21" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(y\\cdot \\left(x^{2}\\right)\\right)=\\left(x^{2}\\right)\\cdot \\left(x e^{2 x^{2}}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495338} {:answer/id #uuid "a0d2a8ac-88e4-519a-a1cd-67d2fbbb3352" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(y\\cdot \\left(e^{- 2 x^{2}}\\right)\\right)=\\left(e^{- 2 x^{2}}\\right)\\cdot \\left(x e^{2 x^{2}}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495350} {:answer/id #uuid "c0f3de7a-6564-5867-82e4-70f297fecd6f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(y\\cdot \\left(e^{- 2 x}\\right)\\right)=\\left(e^{- 2 x}\\right)\\cdot \\left(x e^{2 x^{2}}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495359}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a0d2a8ac-88e4-519a-a1cd-67d2fbbb3352" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(y\\cdot \\left(e^{- 2 x^{2}}\\right)\\right)=\\left(e^{- 2 x^{2}}\\right)\\cdot \\left(x e^{2 x^{2}}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495350} :answer-field/id #uuid "69a0153e-e665-5303-b863-b688cef26fcb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495334}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "a93a7e39-a731-543f-a963-6e7df8a6a066" :question/problem "Consider the following first-order linear ODE for the function $y=y(x):$\n\n$$\n\\left(3\\right)\\cdot \\frac{dy}{dx}-\\left(12 x\\right)\\cdot y=3 x e^{2 x^{2}}\n$$\n\nWrite the equation in the form $\\frac{d}{dx}(yI(x))=I(x)Q(x),$ where $I(x)$ is an integrating factor." :question/worked-solution "First, we write the equation in standard form. This gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}-\\left(4 x\\right)\\cdot y=x e^{2 x^{2}}.\n$$\n\nThis equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}+P(x)y=Q(x)\n$$\n\nwith $P(x)=- 4 x$ and $Q(x)=x e^{2 x^{2}}.$ We proceed to find an integrating factor $I(x)$ using the definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & =e^{\\int P(x)\\,dx} \\\\  & =e^{\\int \\left(- 4 x\\right)\\,dx} \\\\  & =e^{- 2 x^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply our differential equation through by $I(x)=e^{- 2 x^{2}}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\left(e^{- 2 x^{2}}\\right)\\cdot \\left(\\frac{dy}{dx}-\\left(4 x\\right)\\cdot y\\right) & =\\left(e^{- 2 x^{2}}\\right)\\cdot \\left(x e^{2 x^{2}}\\right) \\\\ \\left(e^{- 2 x^{2}}\\right)\\cdot \\frac{dy}{dx}-\\left(4 x\\right)\\cdot \\left(e^{- 2 x^{2}}\\right)\\cdot y & =\\left(e^{- 2 x^{2}}\\right)\\cdot \\left(x e^{2 x^{2}}\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we rewrite the left hand side as $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y\\cdot I(x)):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(y\\cdot \\left(e^{- 2 x^{2}}\\right)\\right) & =\\left(e^{- 2 x^{2}}\\right)\\cdot \\left(x e^{2 x^{2}}\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186495365 :quest