his is the general solution. To find the value of $C$ corresponding to the specific solution, we apply the initial condition $y(0)=-4$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(0) & =\\frac{(6 e^{(0)})+C}{(e^{(0)})} \\\\ -4 & =\\frac{6+C}{1} \\\\ C & =-10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny=6 - 10 e^{- x}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186495481 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "32b482bc-5204-514a-8a0d-f45bc1050dce" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495398} {:answer/id #uuid "6f32642b-9401-5727-8032-5cdc3b514570" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495431} {:answer/id #uuid "caf5a025-9a6f-5e05-ade0-37677d3bc51e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{2 x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495472} {:answer/id #uuid "fdaabce5-51fe-55bc-ad7e-516eab6f6693" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{- x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495494}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6f32642b-9401-5727-8032-5cdc3b514570" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495431} :answer-field/id #uuid "3adaddc6-9b2d-550a-99a5-39a8b4f3752b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495402} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0aa0b6af-c960-571d-91ae-c4512e5f3322" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(5 e^{x} + 6\\right) e^{- x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495379} {:answer/id #uuid "39a4fa50-677e-51d1-b5a8-3236bee613d5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 6 e^{- x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495401} {:answer/id #uuid "3bdc2b72-cb54-533c-b9bd-0c62b01734b7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495403} {:answer/id #uuid "76691e0e-5d65-503f-ad1a-12d8bb485ca8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5 - 6 e^{- x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495433} {:answer/id #uuid "ba3b46e2-99fe-5d65-b50a-dfd440d9f03b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5 e^{x} - 6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495461}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "76691e0e-5d65-503f-ad1a-12d8bb485ca8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5 - 6 e^{- x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495433} :answer-field/id #uuid "dc1dedd2-d5a5-512a-9220-be1c8471e402" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495480}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "dd18b30f-b49b-5ec0-8b50-db3ee61401f9" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem.\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\left(1\\right)y=5,\\quad y(0)=-1\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options below.\n\nAn integrating factor for this equation is $I(x)=$ {{field-1}}.\n\nThe solution to the initial value problem is $y(x)=$ {{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "This equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)y=Q(x),\n$$\n\nwith $P(x)=1$ and $Q(x)=5.$\n\nWe compute an integrating factor using the definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & =e^{\\int P(x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =e^{\\int 1\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =e^{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides of the equation in standard form by $I(x)=e^{x}$ yields\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}e^{x}\\cdot (\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+1y) & =e^{x}\\cdot 5 \\\\ e^{x}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+e^{x}y & =5 e^{x} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(ye^{x}) & =5 e^{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(ye^{x})\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 5 e^{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ ye^{x} & =5\\left(1 e^{x}\\right)+C \\\\ ye^{x} & =5 e^{x}+C \\\\ y & =\\left(C + 5 e^{x}\\right) e^{- x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is the general solution. To find the value of $C$ corresponding to the specific solution, we apply the initial condition $y(0)=-1$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(0) & =\\frac{(5 e^{(0)})+C}{(e^{(0)})} \\\\ -1 & =\\frac{5+C}{1} \\\\ C & =-6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny=5 - 6 e^{- x}.\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Solving First-Order Initial Value Problems Using Integrating Factors"}]}
